        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='container-type:inline-size;width:100%;height:100%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center'><div style='box-sizing:border-box;height:100%;max-width:100%;aspect-ratio:1/1;border-radius:50%;background:#eff6ff;border:4cqmin solid #1e40af;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center'><svg viewBox='0 0 64 64' style='width:62%;height:62%;display:block' aria-hidden='true'><g fill='none' stroke='#1e40af' stroke-width='5' stroke-linecap='round' stroke-linejoin='round'><path d='M32 56V36'/><path d='M32 36L14 16'/><path d='M32 36L50 16'/><path d='M14 28V16H26'/><path d='M38 16H50V28'/></g></svg></div></div>"
        },
        "memo": "The Icon: a fork in the road, for when the decision is seen smaller than a card. The Method writes it.",
        "link": "",
        "reason": "A decision is recognised by its shape, a way that divides: at the size where a card has no room for words, a fork says \"a choice\" at once, and a glyph alone is only a mark."
      }
